  - S4: containment chain in extension_class_containment and extension_regularity_exact matches poset C2 ⊂ C11 ⊂ H2LOC ⊂ C0 (parse the "E_X subset of E_Y" chain pairs).
  - S5: implication_ledger.one_way_entailments: each row's `to` class must be strictly smaller-extension-set than `from` (i.e., E_to ⊂ E_from) given poset; `from`/`to` parsed from "no proper future <TOKEN> extension". Plus the reason's containment claim (if it states "E_A subset of E_B") must match poset. 
  - S6: forbidden_transfers: from/to tokens; the transfer must NOT be licensed (i.e., E_to not strictly contained in E_from). Plus reason must not contain an inverted size premise ("strictly larger"/"strictly smaller") contradicting poset. The F2b D2 defect is precisely here.
  - S7: any denial sentence ("no containment", "no transfer", "not equivalent"?) in normative fields that contradicts an assertion elsewhere: e.g. sentence asserting "no containment with X is asserted" when containment is asserted. Implement as: any occurrence of the phrase pattern `no containment with (C2|C0|...)...(is asserted)` triggers D1 unless scoped as a quoted correction marker (contains "wrong"/"earlier"/"corrected"). The F2a line 152 contains the phrase "the earlier 'no containment with C2 is asserted' was wrong" — that is a mention, not an assertion. So my detector must handle mention contexts; that's exactly the classsep problem. To keep it simple and honest, I'll detect *bare* denial patterns not embedded in quotes and not accompanied by correction markers, and I'll explicitly record the mention contexts. On live F2b it must fire on line 152 (bare denial in must_not_conflate: "No containment with C2 or C0 is asserted here" — likely unquoted). On F2a line 152 the denial is quoted and corrected → not a finding.
  - S8: strength labels: forbidden_strengthenings must list C0/C1/H2loc inextendibility as strength (not weakening); "two-sided" listed as stronger; and forbidden_weakenings must not contain higher-regularity content.
  - S9: cross-reference consistency: `forbidden_transfers` reason for C2→C0 says "converse containment is false" and C2→H2loc similar — consistent.

